    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Hybrid search and incremental loading\n\nTwo independent parts on one canvas.\n\n**Top - loading with change detection.** Google Drive trigger → SHA256 of the file content →\nrow lookup in the `record_manager_hybrid` table → a \"Switch\" into three branches: new file, file\nunchanged, file rewritten. For a changed file the old chunks are deleted first, then the new\nones are loaded. This is a record manager assembled by hand on hashes.\n\n**Bottom - hybrid search as a separate sub-workflow.** Question → embedding → the SQL function\n`match_hybrid_documents_with_details` returns the vector and keyword scores, both ranks\nand the final score → \"Cohere Re-Rank\" reorders the top-10 into the top-5.\n\n### What to replace before running\n\nCredentials (Google Drive, Supabase, Postgres, OpenAI, Cohere), `YOUR_FOLDER_ID` in the trigger,\n`YOUR_WORKFLOW_ID` in the \"Vector Store\" tool node - it points to this same workflow.\nThe tables `hybrid_documents`, `record_manager_hybrid` and the fusion SQL function must be created\nin your own database in advance: they are not in the export.\n\n### What to look at\n\nThe fusion of results happens in the database, and you can see it with your own eyes: the function returns both scores\nand both ranks as separate columns. This is a ready answer to the question of why to keep keyword\nsearch next to vector search.",
        "height": 520,
        "width": 760,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -432,
        -648
      ],
      "id": "74043e20-ab85-49f7-af12-8ea9538257c7",
      "name": "Sticky Note M2"
    }
